From: ohpcd
Subject: [PATCH] fix cmake_install_test API usage

The upstream test calls `boost::json::to_string(value)` but Boost.JSON
1.84.0 only exposes `to_string(kind)`. Switch to `boost::json::serialize`
which accepts `value const&` and produces the same JSON string output.
This makes the cmake_install_test source compile under the OHOS toolchain
so the upstream source inventory (50/50) is fully validated.

--- libs/json/test/cmake_install_test/main.cpp
+++ libs/json/test/cmake_install_test/main.cpp
@@ -12,1 +12,1 @@
-    std::puts(boost::json::to_string(value).c_str());
+    std::puts(boost::json::serialize(value).c_str());

